        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Fustat</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">641 CE – 1168 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founded in 641 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amr-ibn-al-as">Amr ibn al-As</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> in September of that year; according to legend a dove's egg in his tent marked the site.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the eastern bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, just north of the Roman fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, in what is now the Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> district of Cairo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The first capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under Muslim rule; the Mosque of Amr, the first mosque in Egypt; a base for Arab expansion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>; tall residential buildings; pottery and Islamic art; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maimonides">Maimonides</a>; the burning of 1168</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Fustat is a suburb within the Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> district of Cairo, where few buildings remain and the buried remains of the old city are still being excavated.</span></div>
